  "limitations": [
    "Surviving Eanna/Inanna ziggurat constituent of the named Eanna district: mapped irregular lower perimeter, eroded stepped brick core, broad broken shelves, runoff gullies and uneven open crown. No restored summit temple, intact ancient staircase or invented precinct-room grid. Other Eanna remains stay host terrain.",
    "Candidate Q706970 is the Eanna temple complex; its broad reference point is about454m southwest of the standard named Eanna District point35185683624246 and Ziggurat of Uruk point35185683624247. Model only that explicitly reviewed Eanna/Inanna ziggurat constituent at the two overlapping building controls35185683624247/248. Their mapped present-day lower/core outlines fix about74x70m native extent. Native east/south at heading0; mapped architectural axis about0.828849rad, without a signed doorway-facing claim. Broader precinct and other temples are not authored.",
    "About9.6m exposed core above local standard terrain with a low0.85m perimeter remnant. Picture-led height, shelf survival, gully depths, crown level and minor broken ledges are approximate. The model does not restore ancient stages or the vanished summit temple.",
    "Retain the pinned standard Protomaps2026-10-14/Mapzen13–14 six-meter native grid and independent buildings. Lower perimeter and core feet follow sampled grade with buried bottoms; elevated relief is authored exposed masonry/eroded brick, not a copied DEM-only mound. Preserve ground and water; replace only two corresponding native procedural shells with2cm numeric margin. No flattened precinct or ground/water cutout.",
    "Models the explicitly reviewed Eanna/Inanna ziggurat constituent at the named Eanna District controls, not the full temple precinct. Height, shelf survival, erosion slots, crown and low perimeter remnant are visual approximations. No summit temple, ancient staircase, exact brick inventory or buried rooms are restored. Native six-meter terrain limits ground fit."
